<title>USA: TVA Nuclear's Tenn. nuke unit down due pump leak.</title>
<headline>TVA Nuclear's Tenn. nuke unit down due pump leak.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>TVA Nuclear's 1,148 megawatt (MW) Sequoyah nuclear unit 2 in Soddy-Daisy, Tenn., was shut early Friday for unscheduled maintenance, the company said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There was excessive leakage on a seal on a reactor coolant pump,&quot; said company spokeswoman Kay Whittenberg.</p>
<p>She could not comment on the length of the outage but said the outage would be &quot;short-term.&quot;</p>
<p>TVA's other Sequoyah unit, also with a generating capacity of 1,148 MW, is operating at full capacity, she said.</p>
<p>--H McCulloch, New York Power Desk +212-859-1628</p>
